# Extra documentation roots for the docs-targets gate. One directory per line.
#
# COPY THIS TO docs-targets.roots TO USE IT. The live file is gitignored, because
# it names paths on your machine and this repo is public. Sync and back it up by
# whatever means you use for the other trees git is not the system of record for.
#
# The gate's main input is `git ls-files '*.md'`. This file adds trees that live
# OUTSIDE the repo but still issue instructions to whoever reads them: an agent
# memory store, a private notes vault, a sibling docs checkout. Those rot the
# same way a runbook rots, with nobody reviewing them, and a stale one keeps
# issuing a command that no longer exists.
#
# A line naming a directory that is not present is announced and skipped rather
# than failing, because these trees are per-machine and most will be absent on
# most machines. No file here at all means tracked repo docs only, and the gate
# says so when it runs.
#
# Expansions:
#   ~            home directory
#   %REPO_SLUG%  this repo's absolute path with every '/' replaced by '-'
#
# Only the TOP LEVEL of each directory is scanned. Nested directories are left
# alone on purpose, so backup and archive subtrees stay free to name targets
# that are gone.

# Agent memory for this project. Memory carries more authority than a doc: it is
# injected unprompted, and nobody re-reads it the way they re-read a runbook. A
# file in one of these stores was still saying "release with `make
# release_and_push_GHCR`" days after that door was made private, and it was found
# by hand. Another assistant with another layout is one more line, not a code
# change.
# ~/.claude/projects/%REPO_SLUG%/memory

# A sibling checkout or a private notes vault, same idea.
# ~/notes/vaults/this-project
# ../WEB-Sage.Education-docs/docs
